 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Electricity Demand Forecasting & Household Energy Consumption Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook covers:\n",
    "- Data loading & understanding\n",
    "- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "- Household energy usage patterns\n",
    "- Time-series forecasting (ARIMA/SARIMA/ETS, Prophet/LSTM)\n",
    "- Insights & recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Data Loading & Understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "We begin by loading the UCI Individual household electric power consumption dataset. If not present, it will be downloaded automatically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import zipfile\n",
    "import urllib.request\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_URL = 'https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/00235/household_power_consumption.zip'\n",
    "DATA_ZIP = 'household_power_consumption.zip'\n",
    "DATA_TXT = 'household_power_consumption.txt'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Download if not present\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(DATA_TXT):\n",
    "    if not os.path.exists(DATA_ZIP):\n",
    "        print('Downloading dataset...')\n",
    "        urllib.request.urlretrieve(DATA_URL, DATA_ZIP)\n",
    "    print('Extracting dataset...')\n",
    "    with zipfile.ZipFile(DATA_ZIP, 'r') as zip_ref:\n",
    "        zip_ref.extractall('.')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load data\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(\n",
    "    DATA_TXT,\n",
    "    sep=';',\n",
    "    parse_dates={'Datetime': ['Date', 'Time']},\n",
    "    infer_datetime_format=True,\n",
    "    na_values=['?', 'NA'],\n",
    "    low_memory=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Feature Explanations\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature                | Unit         | Description                                                                 |\n",
    "|------------------------|--------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n",
    "| Datetime               | -            | Combined date and time                                                      |\n",
    "| Global_active_power    | kilowatt (kW)| Total active power consumed by the household                                |\n",
    "| Global_reactive_power  | kilowatt (kW)| Total reactive power consumed by the household                              |\n",
    "| Voltage                | volt (V)     | Average voltage measured                                                    |\n",
    "| Global_intensity       | ampere (A)   | Average current intensity                                                   |\n",
    "| Sub_metering_1         | watt-hour    | Kitchen appliances energy consumption (dishwasher, oven, microwave)         |\n",
    "| Sub_metering_2         | watt-hour    | Laundry room appliances (washing machine, dryer, refrigerator, freezer, etc)|\n",
    "| Sub_metering_3         | watt-hour    | Electric water-heater and air-conditioner                                   |\n",
    "\n",
    "- Global_active_power is the main variable for total consumption analysis.\n",
    "- Sub_metering variables allow us to analyze specific household zones.\n",
    "- Voltage and intensity can help detect anomalies or quality issues.\n",
    "- Datetime allows for time-based resampling and trend analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Data info and missing values\n",
    "df.info()\n",
    "print('\nMissing values per column:')\n",
    "print(df.isnull().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time coverage and frequency\n",
    "print(f'\nEarliest timestamp: {df[\'Datetime\'].min()}')\n",
    "print(f'Latest timestamp: {df[\'Datetime\'].max()}')\n",
    "print(f'Total records: {len(df)}')\n",
    "# Calculate frequency (should be 1 min)\n",
    "freq = df['Datetime'].diff().mode()[0]\n",
    "print(f'Most common sampling interval: {freq}')"
   ]
  },
  {
